# Big creature click (BASE.md 29): a creature drawn over more than its own tile (4x4 guardians, world bosses, 2x2 bosses, class looks and mounts wider than a tile, draw scale above 1) takes a click on any of its visible pixels: left/right-click attack, the right-click menu, look, the use-with crosshair, Alt-click attack and Shift-right-click follow, the hotkey crosshair and the action bar's smart cast. Before, only its own (bottom-right) tile did.
#   * ThingType::getTexture keeps a one-bit alpha mask of each creature texture it builds (getAlphaMask(phase), 1/32 of the texture's size).
#   * Outfit::draw records the parts it queues (mount, body, addons; the same parts the outline of 0038 collects; wings and auras do not count) when Creature::draw asks for them; Creature::draw hands MapView one record per drawn creature: its stock one-tile click box, those parts (rect, texture rect, mask), its draw scale (0020) and floor.
#   * MapView keeps the last frame's records in draw order. MapView::getCreatureAt maps a point of the map widget into the framebuffer (zoom and walking camera as getPositionOffset), undoes the draw scale and tests each part's mask; only creatures on the clicked tile's floor or above it count. The topmost one drawn wins; the own character is skipped in that pass and keeps every click that only a big creature's overhang would take. Pure maths in src/client/creaturehit.h (new, header only; tests client/tools/creaturehit_test.cpp, CI).
#   * Lua: UIMap:getCreatureAt(mousePos) (nil when the point is on no creature; the tile's own lookups then apply as before). uigamemap.lua takes it for look, creature and attack (the tile's use thing stays the tile's own, so a use never goes to the creature); onUseWith and the hotkey crosshair prefer it unless the tile's target is a force-use item; onTradeWith and the smart cast use it too. The battle list is unchanged.
#   * Hover: a big creature under the mouse gets the soft outline of 0044 (DrawQueueItemItemOutline, warm white, 2 px) under its largest part. Option "Outline big creatures under the mouse" (bigCreatureHover, on) in a new panel after "Right-click equips items" in Options > Interface; UIMap.setBigCreatureHover(bool) / isBigCreatureHover().
